glum:
And seeks his cab or tram-car homeward bound;
The waiters pass out weary, listless, glum,
To spend their tips on harlots, cards and rum.

De same way in de wintah dat dey do it in de spring;
Dey ain't no use in mopin' 'round an' lookin' mad an' glum
Erbout de wintah season, fu' hit's des plumb boun' to come;

When de fa'mer see him come,
He 'mence lookin' mighty glum,
An' he ketches up a stick;

glue:
Buds will burst their edges,
Strip their wool-coats, glue-coats, streaks,
In the woods and hedges;

gluts:
And nations mix with their primeval dust:
Insatiate still he gluts the ample tomb;
His is the present, his the age to come.
